preConditionHook:
// THE IMPULSE-RETRACEMENT-IMPULSE UNIT MEASURED IN PRICE. Grimes's setup-leg
// strength test (G06-14, G16-21): the leg running NOW -- from the most recent
// confirmed swing pivot low up to this bar's closing price -- is at least
// extensionRatio times the SAME-DIRECTION leg before it, which ran from the
// second swing low up to the swing high between them. The leg that sets up a
// pullback should be at least as strong as the trend's previous legs. Both
// sources read the ratio at 1.0, which is the default. Short is the mirror.
//
// The two-leg form is what is carried: merge decision 14's newest-first scan
// gives two legs per series, so G06-14's average over several prior legs is
// unreachable from Occurrence 1 and 2. SwingLegExceedsAverageLeg is the
// three-pivot averaged sibling and hand-rolls its scan for that reason.
//
// NOT SwingLegLengthAtLeast, which sizes the last two legs in BARS and is
// direction-agnostic; this sizes them in PRICE and compares them to each other.
//
// THE PIVOT SCAN IS INLINED, mirroring the twin's SwingLow / SwingLowBar /
// SwingHigh / SwingHighBar at Occurrence 1 and 2 -- rules in this corpus never
// reference each other. MEASURED (EL_Swing_Probe.txt / el_swing_output1.txt,
// @ES 60 min): the pivot test is MIXED -- AT OR BEYOND the swingStrength OLDER
// bars, STRICTLY BEYOND the swingStrength NEWER bars, and bars-ago indexing
// makes the SMALLER index the NEWER bar, so the strict half is the k < j loop;
// the confirmation lag is exactly swingStrength bars, never 0 or 1, so j starts
// there; pivotLookback is EL's Length with candidate offsets
// 0..pivotLookback-1 inclusive while the neighbourhood test reaches
// swingStrength bars PAST the window, so the deepest index touched is
// pivotLookback - 1 + swingStrength; an empty window is the -1 SENTINEL, which
// the twin guards on the BAR INDEX and this twin reproduces on the same bar
// index, never on a price -- a back-adjusted series can print -1.00 as a real
// price. The comparisons carry the 2.22e-12 relational tolerance. Occurrence 3+
// is UNMEASURED and never asked for. The low side's tie sense is the mirror of
// the measured high-side rule. No WFSafe_SwingLow exists, so plain EL governs.
//
// THE ORDERING GUARD is LegOneEqualsLegTwoTarget's: the anchors must have
// printed in that order for the legs to be legs, so the bars-ago counts descend
// loBar2 > hiBar1 > loBar1 on the long side, and the setup leg must actually be
// up (setupUp > 0, a price DIFFERENCE and so shift-safe).
//
// Written WITHOUT break and with the < 2 counters, statement for statement with
// the twin's Occurrence 1 / 2 reads.
//
// Every scratch value is a localVariables entry rather than a hook-scope
// declaration, so the hooks survive a double placement; the loop counters and
// the per-candidate flags are block-scoped inside the loops.
//
// Deepest bar touched: pivotLookback - 1 + swingStrength.
pivS = (int)swingStrength;
pivW = (int)pivotLookback;
nHi = 0;
nLo = 0;
hiPx1 = -1.0;
hiBar1 = -1.0;
hiPx2 = -1.0;
hiBar2 = -1.0;
loPx1 = -1.0;
loBar1 = -1.0;
loPx2 = -1.0;
loBar2 = -1.0;
for (int j = pivS; j <= pivW - 1; ++j) {
    bool okHi = true;
    bool okLo = true;
    for (int k = j - pivS; k < j; ++k) {
        if (!el_gt(high[j], high[k])) okHi = false;
        if (!el_lt(low[j], low[k])) okLo = false;
    }
    for (int k = j + 1; k <= j + pivS; ++k) {
        if (!el_ge(high[j], high[k])) okHi = false;
        if (!el_le(low[j], low[k])) okLo = false;
    }
    if (okHi && nHi < 2) {
        nHi = nHi + 1;
        if (nHi == 1) { hiPx1 = high[j]; hiBar1 = (double)j; }
        if (nHi == 2) { hiPx2 = high[j]; hiBar2 = (double)j; }
    }
    if (okLo && nLo < 2) {
        nLo = nLo + 1;
        if (nLo == 1) { loPx1 = low[j]; loBar1 = (double)j; }
        if (nLo == 2) { loPx2 = low[j]; loBar2 = (double)j; }
    }
}
setupUp = hiPx1 - loPx2;
runUp = close[0] - loPx1;
setupDn = hiPx2 - loPx1;
runDn = hiPx1 - close[0];
haveUp = (loBar1 != -1.0) && (loBar2 != -1.0) && (hiBar1 != -1.0)
    && el_gt(loBar2, hiBar1) && el_gt(hiBar1, loBar1) && el_gt(setupUp, 0.0);
haveDn = (hiBar1 != -1.0) && (hiBar2 != -1.0) && (loBar1 != -1.0)
    && el_gt(hiBar2, loBar1) && el_gt(loBar1, hiBar1) && el_gt(setupDn, 0.0);
